  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mobility Tracking and Multi-Sectoral Humanitarian Needs in Localities and Sites Affected by Displacement/Return in the Central African Republic (National Coverage)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In the context of the protracted crisis generating continuous displacements in the Central African Republic, the Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM), deployed since 2013, makes it possible to collect, analyze and share information concerning displacements and returns, as well as multisectoral conditions and needs of affected populations, in order to guide decision-making and the definition of humanitarian responses. There continues to be a need for nationwide updates on the situation of displacement and the needs it generates for affected populations. Thus, the project will extend and perpetuate its activities in the prefectures of the country not yet covered and in all the camp coordination and camp management displacement sites that do not have managers.</narrative>
  </description>
